sub:assertion {
    <https://w3id.org/delphi/resource/claim/morphoeval-delphi10000-drosophila-biarmipes-turing-wavelength-s0> pk:hasAssessment <https://w3id.org/delphi/resource/assessment/morphoeval-delphi10000-drosophila-biarmipes-turing-wavelength-s0-overall> .
    <https://w3id.org/delphi/resource/assessment/morphoeval-delphi10000-drosophila-biarmipes-turing-wavelength-s0-overall> a pk:LLMClaimAssessment ;
        rdfs:label "Drosophila biarmipes Turing wavelength at 1.5 µm (detail s0, 0 Ma) — MorphoEval overall 83.7/100" ;
        dct:date "2026-10-27"^^xsd:date ;
        dct:description "Schnakenberg reaction-diffusion on a 17.832 µm periodic patch. Linear lambda_c = 1.486 µm (the catalog 1.5 µm detail scale), sigma_max = 0.391. Predecessor D. ananassae is subcritical (sigma_max = -0.538) at the same diffusivities. Successor D. bipectinata selects 1.400 µm. Equal-diffusion ablation has sigma_max = -0.102. Pearson r of linearised growth rates against analytical sigma(k) is 0.9998 (RMSE 0.0037). The saturated 96² lattice centroid is 1.259 µm, 15% shorter than lambda_c; that gap is the open remediation. GIF 720×540, 12 frames, cv_sim_similarity 82.3 against the species-gallery plate. Gompel 2005 did not measure 1.5 µm. Overall 83.7/100 (faithfulness 83.0, reproducibility 85.5); rubric morphoeval 0.1.0; checkpoint commit 0c76d15d14afcec6c366e1b9274a6586a0de48fc; environment: . Dimension assessments: Model fidelity to source 86, Morphological realism / specimen match 78, Parameter expressivity 88, Morphometric validation 84, Source and data traceability 86, Code-to-model traceability 84, Reproducibility package 86. Output judged: docs/media/drosophila_biarmipes_turing_wavelength_s0_comparison.png: rendered output of models/2026-delphi10000-drosophila-biarmipes-turing-wavelength-s0.py at 0c76d15d14afcec6c366e1b9274a6586a0de48fc, image/png, 635372 B, 1512×1104 px, artifact_sha256 cc98bff5da7b5bce905d2f461aa6439d286cdb75c6b71e1bf8c1a57918414fd7 (sha256 cc98bff5da7b5bce905d2f461aa6439d286cdb75c6b71e1bf8c1a57918414fd7), spec_fingerprint 92a782c52c8ca9f615d1f1bd608e11b29abe77968c127a57fb11ff06573e3b27. Dual provenance: spec_fingerprint: 92a782c52c8ca9f615d1f1bd608e11b29abe77968c127a57fb11ff06573e3b27; artifact_sha256: cc98bff5da7b5bce905d2f461aa6439d286cdb75c6b71e1bf8c1a57918414fd7; input_dataset_sha256: {datasets/drosophila_biarmipes_turing_wavelength_s0/drosophila_biarmipes_specimen.jpg=02b2cb2ee9a1dfe4..., datasets/drosophila_biarmipes_turing_wavelength_s0/drosophila_biarmipes_turing_wavelength_s0_reference.json=7a8e083bfed7c064..., datasets/drosophila_biarmipes_turing_wavelength_s0/paper_citations.bib=703e65d53e861547..., datasets/drosophila_biarmipes_turing_wavelength_s0/scout_manifest.json=eba9988ac4767d3e...}. Claim boundary: reported_in_source: Gompel et al. 2005: D. biarmipes males deploy a novel yellow wing-spot enhancer. | Prud'homme et al. 2006: wing spots evolved repeatedly via yellow cis-regulatory elements. | Turing 1952: a finite critical wavenumber when the inhibitor diffuses faster than the activator.; reconstructed_in_script: Schnakenberg (a, b, D_u, D_v) whose linear lambda_c equals 1.486 µm. | Ananassae subcritical and bipectinata shorter-wavelength shifts at fixed diffusivities.; transfer_boundary: 1.5 µm is the Delphi 3_subcellular_um assignment, not a length reported by Gompel. | Chronoseries neighbors are catalog positions 5 and 7, not a phylogenetic ancestor chain.; does_not_claim: That yellow transcription is Schnakenberg kinetics. | That the gallery plate is a micrograph of a 1.5 µm melanin lattice. | That D. ananassae gave rise to D. biarmipes which gave rise to D. bipectinata.." ;
        dct:subject <https://w3id.org/delphi/resource/concept/morphoeval-rubric-0.1.0> ;
        pk:assessedBy <https://w3id.org/delphi/resource/model/grok-4.7> ;
        pk:assessmentType "morphoeval/0.1.0/overall" ;
        pk:evidenceAgainst "open need [specimen_comparison/specimen-match, pressure P=1.8]: A CC-licensed micrograph of D. biarmipes wing-spot cuticle at ~1 µm resolution. Wikimedia had no bitmap on 2026-10-27; the gallery plate is the fallback.",
            "remediation needed: R1: Re-measure the nonlinear spectral centroid on a 128² grid. The 96² centroid is 1.259 µm against linear lambda_c 1.486 µm, and this pass cannot tell grid locking from a real nonlinear shift.",
            "remediation needed: R2: Put linear lambda_c, the 96² centroid, and the 128² centroid on the comparison figure next to the dispersion curve." ;
        pk:hasScore "0.837"^^xsd:double ;
        pk:hasVerdict "faithful" .
    <https://w3id.org/delphi/resource/model/grok-4.7> a pk:Model ;
        rdfs:label "Grok 4.7 (builder-assessor, single-agent Pass 1)" ;
        dct:identifier "grok-4.7" ;
        prov:actedOnBehalfOf <https://orcid.org/0009-0007-4948-9192> .
}

